Let's look at the number of bags a single person carries. A single person carries $y$ bags every trip and does $2$ trips. So in total, the person carries $2y$ bags:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\left(y\,\dfrac{\text{bags}}{\text{trip}}\right)\left(2\,\text{trips}\right)
\\\\
&=2y\,\dfrac{\text{bags}}{\cancel{\text{trip}}}\cdot\,\cancel{\text{trips}}
\\\\
&=2y\,\text{bags}
\end{align}$
